<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Lesson 2a: The Narrative of the Graph — KS3 Skills</title>
<style>
  :root{
    /* Analytical Blue Theme */
    --bg:#fafaf7;
    --ink:#23332b;
    --muted:#5a6b62;
    --leaf:#2B5EA7;      /* Primary Blue */
    --leaf-dk:#1A365D;   /* Dark Blue */
    --leaf-soft:#EBF4FF; /* Light Blue */
    --leaf-line:#BEE3F8; /* Border Blue */
    --sky:#eef4fb;
    --sky-line:#cfe0f0;
    --sky-dk:#3a6594;
    --sun:#fff6e3;
    --sun-line:#f0d9a3;
    --sun-dk:#8a6614;
    --rose:#fdeeee;
    --rose-line:#f2c7c7;
    --plum:#f1ebfa;
    --plum-line:#dccff0;
    --plum-dk:#5a3a8a;
    --chip:#f1ede4;
    --shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.04), 0 6px 18px rgba(43,94,167,.08);
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box}
  html,body{margin:0;padding:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);
    font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Inter,Roboto,sans-serif;
    line-height:1.55;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
  .wrap{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;padding:28px 24px 80px}

  header.hero{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#ffffff 0%,#f4f8fc 100%);
    border:1px solid var(--leaf-line);border-radius:18px;padding:22px 26px;
    box-shadow:var(--shadow);margin-bottom:18px}
  .eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--leaf);font-weight:600}
  h1{font-size:28px;margin:6px 0 4px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
  .sub{color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px;margin:0 0 14px}

  .picker{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;align-items:center;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--leaf-line);border-radius:14px;padding:10px 12px}
  .picker .pick-label{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-right:4px}
  .picker button{appearance:none;border:1px solid var(--leaf-line);background:#fff;color:var(--ink);
    border-radius:999px;padding:7px 14px;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;transition:.15s}
  .picker button:hover{background:var(--leaf-soft)}
  .picker button.active{background:var(--leaf);color:#fff;border-color:var(--leaf)}
  .picker .reset{margin-left:auto;background:transparent;border:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:12.5px;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:underline}

  /* MASTER CODE */
  .master{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--leaf-line);border-radius:14px;padding:14px 16px;margin-top:14px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:14px}
  .master-label{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}
  .code{display:flex;gap:6px}
  .code .slot{width:34px;height:42px;border:1.5px dashed #cfd2c4;border-radius:8px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:800;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:18px;color:#bdb999;background:#fbfaf3;transition:.25s}
  .code .slot.unlocked{border-style:solid;border-color:var(--leaf);background:var(--leaf-soft);color:var(--leaf-dk);transform:rotateY(0)}
  .master-hint{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin-left:auto}

  /* PROGRESS DOTS */
  .progress{display:flex;gap:6px;margin-top:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .pdot{flex:1;min-width:18px;height:8px;background:#e2e8f0;border-radius:6px;transition:.2s}
  .pdot.done{background:var(--leaf)}
  .progress-meta{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px;text-align:right}

  .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 290px;gap:20px;margin-top:8px}
  @media (max-width:880px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}

  section.card{background:#fff;border:1px solid #ecebe4;border-radius:16px;
    padding:20px 22px;margin-bottom:16px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);transition:.2s}
  section.card.done{background:#f8fafc;border-color:var(--leaf-line)}
  .sec-head{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px}
  .sec-num{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:26px;height:26px;
    background:var(--leaf);color:#fff;border-radius:8px;font-weight:700;font-size:13px}
  .sec-title{font-size:17px;font-weight:700;margin:0}
  .time{margin-left:auto;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;
    background:var(--chip);color:#665a3f;border-radius:999px;padding:4px 10px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600}
  .time::before{content:"";width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#d8b85a;display:inline-block}
  .task{font-size:15px;margin:4px 0 10px}

  .toggles{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin:10px 0 0}
  .tog{appearance:none;border:1px solid #e0dccd;background:#fff;border-radius:999px;
    padding:6px 12px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;transition:.15s}
  .tog:hover{background:#fafaf2}
  .tog.help{color:var(--sky-dk);border-color:var(--sky-line)}
  .tog.help.on{background:var(--sky);border-color:var(--sky-dk)}
  .tog.stem{color:var(--plum-dk);border-color:var(--plum-line)}
  .tog.stem.on{background:var(--plum);border-color:var(--plum-dk)}
  .tog.stretch{color:var(--sun-dk);border-color:var(--sun-line)}
  .tog.stretch.on{background:var(--sun);border-color:var(--sun-dk)}
  .tog.unlock{color:var(--leaf-dk);border-color:var(--leaf-line)}
  .tog.unlock.on{background:var(--leaf-soft);border-color:var(--leaf-dk)}
  .tog.done{margin-left:auto;color:var(--leaf-dk);border-color:var(--leaf-line)}
  .tog.done.on{background:var(--leaf);color:#fff;border-color:var(--leaf)}

  .panel{display:none;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 14px;margin-top:10px;border:1px solid;font-size:14.5px}
  .panel.show{display:block;animation:slide .18s ease-out}
  @keyframes slide{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(-4px)}to{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0)}}
  .panel.help{background:var(--sky);border-color:var(--sky-line)}
  .panel.stem{background:var(--plum);border-color:var(--plum-line)}
  .panel.stretch{background:var(--sun);border-color:var(--sun-line)}
  .panel .label{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:4px}
  .panel.help .label{color:var(--sky-dk)}
  .panel.stem .label{color:var(--plum-dk)}
  .panel.stretch .label{color:var(--sun-dk)}

  /* LOCK PANEL */
  .lockbox{display:none;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin-top:10px;border:1.5px solid var(--leaf-line);background:linear-gradient(180deg,#ffffff 0%, #f4f8fc 100%)}
  .lockbox.show{display:block;animation:slide .18s ease-out}
  .lockbox .label{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:var(--leaf-dk);margin-bottom:6px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}
  .riddle{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink);margin:6px 0 10px;font-style:italic;line-height:1.5}
  .keyrow{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;align-items:center}
  .keyrow input{flex:1;min-width:160px;border:1.5px solid var(--leaf-line);background:#fff;border-radius:10px;padding:9px 12px;font-size:14.5px;font-family:inherit;outline:none;transition:.15s}
  .keyrow input:focus{border-color:var(--leaf-dk);background:#fff}
  .keyrow input.wrong{border-color:#c97070;background:#fdf6f6}
  .keyrow input.right{border-color:var(--leaf);background:var(--leaf-soft)}
  .keyrow .check-btn{appearance:none;border:0;background:var(--leaf);color:#fff;border-radius:10px;padding:9px 16px;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;transition:.15s}
  .keyrow .hint-btn{appearance:none;border:1px solid var(--leaf-line);background:#fff;color:var(--leaf-dk);border-radius:10px;padding:8px 12px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer}
  .feedback{font-size:13px;margin-top:8px;min-height:18px}
  .feedback.wrong{color:#a84a4a}
  .feedback.right{color:var(--leaf-dk);font-weight:700}
  .answers{display:none;margin-top:12px;padding:12px 14px;background:#fff;border:1px dashed var(--leaf-line);border-radius:10px;font-size:14.5px}
  .answers.unlocked{display:block;animation:slide .25s ease-out}

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12px 0; font-size: 14.5px; }
  th { background: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 700; text-align: left; padding: 8px 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; font-size: 13px; color: var(--leaf-dk); }
  td { padding: 8px 10px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 13.5px; }

  aside.glossary{position:sticky;top:14px;align-self:start;background:#fff;border:1px solid #ecebe4;
    border-radius:16px;padding:16px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);max-height:calc(100vh - 28px);overflow:auto}
  aside.glossary h3{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--leaf)}
  .kw{display:grid;grid-template-columns:34px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:start;margin:9px 0;padding-bottom:9px;border-bottom:1px dashed #eee}
  .kw .ic{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:9px;background:var(--leaf-soft);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;color:var(--leaf-dk);}
  .kw .term{font-weight:700;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.25}
  .kw .def{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:2px}

  .celebrate{display:none;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ebf4ff 0%,#fff6e3 100%);border:1px solid var(--leaf-line);border-radius:14px;padding:18px;text-align:center;margin-bottom:16px;color:var(--leaf-dk);font-weight:600}
  .celebrate.show{display:block}
  .celebrate .big{font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:28px;letter-spacing:.4em;font-weight:800;display:block;margin:6px 0;color:var(--leaf-dk)}

  .plenary-fill{display:grid;gap:8px;margin-top:10px}
  .pfill{background:#fff;border:1px solid #ecebe4;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 12px;font-size:14.5px;cursor:pointer;transition:.15s}
  .pfill .ans{display:none;color:var(--leaf-dk);font-weight:700;margin-top:6px}
  .pfill.flipped .ans{display:block;animation:slide .18s ease-out}

  .salt-box{background:#f8fafc; border:1px solid var(--leaf-line); border-radius:12px; padding:14px; margin:14px 0;}
  .salt-box b{color:var(--leaf); font-size:18px; display:inline-block; width:20px;}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <header class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">KS3 Science · Working Scientifically</div>
    <h1>The Narrative of the Graph 📉</h1>
    <p class="sub">Data tells a story, but only if you choose the right visual. Today we master <b>graph selection</b> and the <b>S.A.L.T. framework</b> for precision plotting.</p>

    <div class="picker">
      <span class="pick-label">Pick your support level →</span>
      <button id="lvl-light" class="lvl">🚀 I've got this</button>
      <button id="lvl-std" class="lvl active">⚖️ Standard</button>
      <button id="lvl-full" class="lvl">🪜 Give me all the support</button>
      <button class="reset" id="reset">Reset progress</button>
    </div>

    <div class="master">
      <span class="master-label">🔑 Master code</span>
      <div class="code" id="codeBoxes"></div>
      <span class="master-hint">Crack each section's keyword to reveal a letter. Solve all 6 to spell today's key theme.</span>
    </div>

    <div class="progress" id="progress"></div>
    <div class="progress-meta"><span id="done-count">0</span> / <span id="total-count">6</span> sections done</div>
  </header>

  <div class="celebrate" id="celebrate">
    ✨ Master code cracked! The word was…
    <span class="big">GRAPHS</span>
    You are ready to turn raw numbers into scientific evidence.
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <main>

      <section class="card" data-sec="1" data-keyword="independent" data-letter="G" data-letter-idx="0">
        <div class="sec-head">
          <span class="sec-num">1</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title">Activate — X marks the spot</h2>
          <span class="time">5 min</span>
        </div>
        <p class="task">In Lesson 1, we learned that the IV always goes in the first column. On a graph, the <b>Independent Variable (IV)</b> always goes on the <b>X-axis</b> (the horizontal one).</p>
        
        <div style="background:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius:12px; padding:14px;">
          <b>Scenario: Heating Water</b><br>
          A student measures the <b>temperature</b> of water every <b>60 seconds</b> as it is heated by a Bunsen burner.
        </div>

        <div class="toggles">
          <button class="tog help">💡 Help me identify</button>
          <button class="tog stretch">⚡ Stretch</button>
          <button class="tog unlock">🔒 Unlock check</button>
          <button class="tog done">✓ I've done this</button>
        </div>

        <div class="panel help"><div class="label">Variables Reminder</div>
          <p><b>IV (Independent):</b> What did the student decide to change/set? (Hint: The clock kept ticking...)</p>
          <p><b>DV (Dependent):</b> What changed <i>because</i> of the heat? What was written in the table?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel stretch"><div class="label">Push yourself</div>
          <p>If you were to plot this, what would be the <b>labels</b> for your X and Y axes, including the units?</p>
        </div>

        <div class="lockbox">
          <div class="label">🔒 Riddle to unlock</div>
          <p class="riddle">"I am the variable that goes on the horizontal X-axis. I am the thing 'I change' or set. What am I? (11 letters)"</p>
          <div class="keyrow">
            <input type="text" placeholder="Type the keyword…">
            <button class="check-btn">Check</button>
          </div>
          <div class="feedback"></div>
          <div class="answers">
            <div class="alabel">✓ Answers</div>
            <p><b>IV (X-axis):</b> Time (seconds)<br><b>DV (Y-axis):</b> Temperature (°C)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="card" data-sec="2" data-keyword="continuous" data-letter="R" data-letter-idx="1">
        <div class="sec-head">
          <span class="sec-num">2</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title">The Selection Matrix</h2>
          <span class="time">8 min</span>
        </div>
        <p class="task">You must choose between a <b>Bar Chart</b> and a <b>Line Graph</b>. The choice depends on the <i>type</i> of data.</p>

        <div class="salt-box" style="background:#ebf4ff;">
          <p>📊 <b>Bar Charts</b> are for <b>Categorical</b> data (words or distinct groups). Bars must not touch!</p>
          <p>📈 <b>Line Graphs</b> are for <b>Continuous</b> data (measurements that can be any value, like time or length).</p>
        </div>

        <p class="task"><b>Task:</b> Decide which graph you would use for these 3 datasets:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A: Number of students with different eye colours.</li>
          <li>B: The height of a bean plant measured every day for a week.</li>
          <li>C: The boiling point of different types of alcohol.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="toggles">
          <button class="tog help">💡 Decision Hint</button>
          <button class="tog stretch">⚡ Stretch</button>
          <button class="tog unlock">🔒 Unlock check</button>
          <button class="tog done">✓ I've done this</button>
        </div>

        <div class="panel help"><div class="label">Hint</div>
          <p>If the data is <b>words</b> (Brown, Blue, Green), use a <b>Bar Chart</b>. If the data is <b>numbers</b> that come from measuring, use a <b>Line Graph</b>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel stretch"><div class="label">Push yourself</div>
          <p>Shoe size is numerical (4, 5, 6), but you can't be a size 5.234. Is this discrete or continuous? Which graph would a scientist use?</p>
        </div>

        <div class="lockbox">
          <div class="label">🔒 Riddle to unlock</div>
          <p class="riddle">"I am data that can be any numerical value on a scale. I usually require a line graph. What am I? (10 letters)"</p>
          <div class="keyrow">
            <input type="text" placeholder="Type the keyword…">
            <button class="check-btn">Check</button>
          </div>
          <div class="feedback"></div>
          <div class="answers">
            <div class="alabel">✓ Answers</div>
            <p><b>A:</b> Bar Chart (Categorical)<br><b>B:</b> Line Graph (Continuous)<br><b>C:</b> Bar Chart (Categorical - "Types" are categories)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="card" data-sec="3" data-keyword="scale" data-letter="A" data-letter-idx="2">
        <div class="sec-head">
          <span class="sec-num">3</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title">The S.A.L.T. Framework</h2>
          <span class="time">7 min</span>
        </div>
        <p class="task">To get full marks in an exam, every graph must follow the <b>S.A.L.T.</b> rules. Memorise these now.</p>

        <div class="salt-box">
          <p><b>S</b> — <b>Scale:</b> Must go up in equal steps and cover at least 50% of the grid.</p>
          <p><b>A</b> — <b>Axes:</b> IV on X, DV on Y. Use a ruler!</p>
          <p><b>L</b> — <b>Labels:</b> Must match your table headers EXACTLY, including units.</p>
          <p><b>T</b> — <b>Title:</b> "A graph to show how [IV] affects [DV]".</p>
        </div>

        <div class="toggles">
          <button class="tog help">💡 Scale Tips</button>
          <button class="tog stretch">⚡ Stretch</button>
          <button class="tog unlock">🔒 Unlock check</button>
          <button class="tog done">✓ I've done this</button>
        </div>

        <div class="panel help"><div class="label">Scale Tips</div>
          <p>Good scales use multiples of 1, 2, 5, or 10. Avoid "awkward" scales like going up in 3s or 7s—it makes plotting nearly impossible!</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel stretch"><div class="label">Push yourself</div>
          <p>Explain why a scale that only uses the bottom corner of the graph paper is considered "Bad Science".</p>
        </div>

        <div class="lockbox">
          <div class="label">🔒 Riddle to unlock</div>
          <p class="riddle">"In SALT, I am the letter that ensures your graph isn't too small and goes up in even steps. What am I? (5 letters)"</p>
          <div class="keyrow">
            <input type="text" placeholder="Type the keyword…">
            <button class="check-btn">Check</button>
          </div>
          <div class="feedback"></div>
          <div class="answers">
            <div class="alabel">✓ Secure</div>
            <p>If your scale is too small, you cannot see the <b>precision</b> of the data or identify anomalies easily. Always aim for "Big and Bold".</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="card" data-sec="4" data-keyword="pencil" data-letter="P" data-letter-idx="3">
        <div class="sec-head">
          <span class="sec-num">4</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title">Face-to-Face Plotting Challenge</h2>
          <span class="time">15 min</span>
        </div>
        <p class="task"><b>Hand-draw</b> a line graph using the data below. This shows how water heats up with the Bunsen air-hole <b>slightly open</b> vs <b>fully open</b>. <i>(From Skills Sheet 4)</i></p>

        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Time (s)</th>
              <th>Temp (Slightly Open) / °C</th>
              <th>Temp (Fully Open) / °C</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>0</td><td>22</td><td>22</td></tr>
            <tr><td>120</td><td>33</td><td>42</td></tr>
            <tr><td>240</td><td>41</td><td>61</td></tr>
            <tr><td>360</td><td>52</td><td>83</td></tr>
            <tr><td>480</td><td>62</td><td>100</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <div class="toggles">
          <button class="tog help">💡 Plotting Tips</button>
          <button class="tog stem">📚 Drawing Checklist</button>
          <button class="tog stretch">⚡ Stretch</button>
          <button class="tog unlock">🔒 Unlock check</button>
          <button class="tog done">✓ I've done this</button>
        </div>

        <div class="panel help"><div class="label">Plotting Tips</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Use a <b>sharp pencil</b> and mark points with a small 'x', not a big blob.</li>
            <li>Plot both sets of data on the same grid. Use a <b>Key</b> to show which line is which.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="panel stem"><div class="label">Checklist</div>
          <ul class="stems">
            <li>Scale: X goes to 480, Y goes to 100.</li>
            <li>Labels: Time (s) on X, Temperature (°C) on Y.</li>
            <li>Ruler: Are your axes and lines of best fit perfectly straight?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="panel stretch"><div class="label">Push yourself</div>
          <p>Calculate the <b>Rate of Heating</b> for the 'Fully Open' burner. (Change in Temp ÷ Time taken).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="lockbox">
          <div class="label">🔒 Riddle to unlock</div>
          <p class="riddle">"I must be sharp. If you use a pen to draw a graph, I am what you'll wish you had when you make a mistake. What am I? (6 letters)"</p>
          <div class="keyrow">
            <input type="text" placeholder="Type the keyword…">
            <button class="check-btn">Check</button>
          </div>
          <div class="feedback"></div>
          <div class="answers">
            <div class="alabel">✓ Plotting Gold Standard</div>
            <p>Check your graph: Does the 'Fully Open' line have a steeper gradient (slope)? It should, as it heats the water faster.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="card" data-sec="5" data-keyword="units" data-letter="H" data-letter-idx="4">
        <div class="sec-head">
          <span class="sec-num">5</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title">Audit — Spot the Error</h2>
          <span class="time">7 min</span>
        </div>
        
        <p class="task">A student investigated adding Zinc to Copper Sulphate. Look at the data from their table (<i>Sheet 10</i>) and <b>identify 3 errors</b>.</p>

        <div style="background:#fff; border:2px solid var(--rose-line); border-radius:12px; padding:12px; margin-bottom:12px; color:#b91c1c;">
          <b>Student Table:</b><br>
